# IL TURNO COMPOSTO — gen506b/gen506c.
#
# Il banco di comprensione (tests/comprehension-probe) e' fatto di turni con
# piu' clausole e una domanda alla fine. Misurato sulla baseline: sette su
# trentadue li prendeva `smalltalk` per una cue («can you», «your») e
# rispondeva «I don't have any of my own — I'm parrot0, an AI»; altri quattro
# li prendeva un frame di analisi ripetendo il prompt intero; quattro tenevano
# il demone oltre i due minuti dentro il muro (una regola O(n^4) sui nodi).
#
# gen506b ha dato un nome al turno composto (`compound_inquiry`, turn-frames.p0)
# e un muro che nomina la forma. gen506c segue il consiglio di quel muro da
# solo: il turno si spezza alle superfici di confine dichiarate in KB e OGNI
# clausola e' letta dal lettore di un turno intero — chi insegna insegna, chi
# chiede risponde o mura, e il muro nomina la clausola, non una parola a caso.
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=1
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!timeout 8
!reset

[test la lettura: piu' clausole, ognuna letta come un turno]
!timeout 8
> Every giraffe in this reserve is spotted, and Kibo is a giraffe that lives in the reserve. Does the spot pattern on Kibo follow from those two facts alone, and is there any way Kibo could be plain?
<~ Learned: kibo is a giraffe
<~ I couldn't read «
<! I don't have any of my own
<! several statements and a question
!query giraffe(kibo)
!query turn_illocution(current_turn, compound_inquiry)
!query turn_cue(current_turn, clause_boundary_cue, $B)

[test il registro sociale non ruba un turno composto, e un quantificatore non universale non diventa un individuo]
!reset
!timeout 8
> No mechanic here is a pilot, but several pilots are sailors. Could a sailor who works here also be a mechanic, and can you say whether every sailor is a pilot?
<~ nothing is both mechanic here and pilot
<~ I can't hold «several pilots are sailors»
<! several pilots is a sailor
<! I don't have any of my own
<! Want me to learn about it
!query! sailor(several_pilots)

[test un turno che era appeso torna in secondi]
!reset
!timeout 8
> Assume for a moment that all feathers are heavy. A feather from this nest is lying on the table, and the table is in a museum. Given that assumption, must the feather be heavy, and what would a scale prove about the real world?
<~ table is located in museum
<~ I couldn't read «

[test una domanda semplice NON e' un turno composto]
!reset
> what is the capital of france
< Paris.
!query! turn_illocution(current_turn, compound_inquiry)

# La domanda sulla CLASSE si prova per testimone, e la formula di richiesta
# davanti e' un involucro, non contenuto (question_wrapper/1, grammar.p0).
[test la classe generica e universale si prova per testimone; l'involucro si toglie]
!reset
!timeout 8
> every sailor is a pilot
<~ Learned rule
> is a sailor a pilot?
< Yes.
> is every sailor a pilot?
< Yes.
> can you say whether every sailor is a pilot?
< Yes.
> every sailor is a pilot?
<! Learned
<! Got it
!forget question_wrapper("can you say whether")
> can you say whether every sailor is a pilot?
<! Yes.
!assert question_wrapper("can you say whether")

# Il modificatore non si butta: «all calm pilots are trusted» e' una regola a
# corpo congiunto, non «every pilot is trusted». E il testimone della domanda
# sulla classe riceve un fatto per ogni parola del soggetto.
[test il modificatore resta nella regola, e il testimone lo porta]
!reset
!timeout 8
> all calm pilots are trusted
<~ if something is a calm pilot, then it is trusted
> bob is a pilot
> is bob trusted?
<! Yes.
> bob is calm
> is bob trusted?
< Yes.
> is it true that every calm pilot is trusted?
< Yes.
> does it follow that bob is trusted?
< Yes.

# Ablazione: se nessuna superficie separa le clausole, il turno non e'
# composto e non viene letto per clausole — la lettura e' conoscenza.
[test ablazione: senza le superfici di confine il turno non e' composto]
!reset
!timeout 8
!forget clause_boundary_cue(", and ")
!forget clause_boundary_cue(", but ")
!forget clause_boundary_cue(". ")
> No mechanic here is a pilot, but several pilots are sailors. Could a sailor who works here also be a mechanic, and can you say whether every sailor is a pilot?
<! nothing is both mechanic here and pilot
!query! turn_illocution(current_turn, compound_inquiry)
!assert clause_boundary_cue(", and ")
!assert clause_boundary_cue(", but ")
!assert clause_boundary_cue(". ")
